compiler plans ignore probe paths and GCC's derived dump names: true
compiler plan normalization retains SDK paths and effective flags: true
the census models GCC/GAS and Clang assembly on x86-64 and aarch64: true
both arm64 dialects' instructions are classified, not only their loops found: true
a libm call spelled the Mach-O way is still counted as one: true
clang line attribution is found through the construct range, not the exact anchor line: true
the fp8 combine selector rejects a deliberate libm regression outside its codec loop: true
an instruction in an unknown dialect is reported as residual: true
the brace range alone reads the staging loop gcc nested beside the accumulator: true
the exact source anchor reads the accumulator loop: true
a census row takes its exact source anchor ahead of the brace-range fallback: true
residual mnemonics count only unclassified instructions, ordered by frequency: true
residual display breaks frequency ties by mnemonic and bounds the omitted total: true
a fully classified listing has an empty residual diagnostic: true
vector FMAs are counted with their register widths in every dialect, and scalar FMAs and packed multiplies are not: true
a memory operand through the stack or frame pointer is a stack reference, a register is not: true
a memory operand through %rbp is a stack reference only in a function that made %rbp its frame pointer: true
a stack write is a store to the stack in either dialect, a reload or a compare is not: true
line attribution reads the instructions under a line's .loc, across a label, and no other line's or file's: true
a scalar move from memory is a load, not scalar FP work, and an x-suffixed AVX512-FP16 conversion is packed: true
